{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792364580,"nonce":"Kf6cSpl07svd93CFxT+4wulbIyM=","title":"A page with a large path canvas, left and visited again, keeps tens of MB per visit alive","message":"**What happens**\n\nIn the web dashboard (apps/dashboard), each visit to the Navigate page, whose canvas draws a street map of thousands of paths, adds about 40-60 MB to what the collector reports live, and it is not given back after the page is left. After about ten visits the 512 MiB heap is full and the page spends its time collecting. The other pages stay flat. aa0105a avoids it in the app by keeping the map's canvas built (Canvas retain, 79e0b2d); the cause is not fixed.\n\n**Reproducer**\n\ngit checkout 2fe21bf -- apps/dashboard/src/dashboard/Dashboard.hx apps/dashboard/src/dashboard/NavigateView.hx haxe/ashui/ui/Canvas.hx haxe/ashui/core/render/CanvasPainter.hx, build the dashboard for the web (tests/wasm/run.sh Dashboard), open it with ?env=ASH_GC_STATS=1 and click Navigate and More alternately: the live heap goes 57, 130, 179, 243, 322 MB over five laps.\n\n**What was measured**\n\n- Counts of live things stay flat through the laps: timers in the scheduler 2-3, undisposed Owners 24, undisposed CanvasPainters 5. So no Owner, Timer or painter accumulates; the memory is held through something a disposed page leaves behind.\n- ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS chains for the 16-18 MB objects are ordinary reachability: root slot, ThemeState, AnimationScheduler, its timer array, a pending release Timer, the CanvasPainter it releases, its Canvas and that Canvas's Owner, a children array, a second Canvas, its CanvasPainter, the shapes IntMap, a Path, an array, the big buffer. 37 of 42 chains over 5 MB pass through a Timer, 39 through a CanvasPainter. Others end at VehicleView, its Ref, a SignalDynamic and a Canvas.\n- Ash's collector side was checked by its session: the earlier gc-verify warnings were its own verifier reading a class's runtime object as an instance; the collector behaves as it should.\n- Releasing the painter's buffers in CanvasPainter.dispose, typed layers in StreetMap, and splitting the map into a base and an overlay each made no difference.\n\n**What to look at next**\n\nWhat keeps the previous visit's Canvas, with its Owner subtree, reachable from the pending release Timer or from VehicleView's Ref; whether a Canvas holds its painter and its Owner after dispose; whether the shapes cache of a disposed painter needs clearing in dispose (the release Timer clears it only when it fires).","files":null}]}